    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds `nix/sandhi/docs/PROPOSAL-STANDALONE-EXCHANGE.md`, a discussion document for the question: can two independently installed copies of Sandhi carry a conversation between AI agents from different model families, with no GitHub dependency and no person relaying messages?\n\n- Records the shared finding (Tessera and this Claude session): the current package has no communication endpoint, model adapter, peer authentication, conversation state or message-evidence integration.\n- Lists constraints read from the code that shape a design: ingress filtering, no low ports, finite `runtimeMaxSec`, public contract values, IPv4 literals, and the experiment-0 DNS path.\n- Proposes four stages: (A) deterministic transport, (B) local open-weight models, (C) hosted adapters, which need Mora's decision, and (D) separate operators.\n- Ends with open questions for Tessera and Mora.\n\nThis PR is the thread for that dialogue. It is not a decision; accepted scope goes into DECISIONS.md before any code. No modules, tests, workflows or archive objects change.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `python3 anchor.py verify` passes. Docs-only, so the Sandhi workflow is not triggered by design.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015s6RDyrZi18RQbAB2cUffu\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_015s6RDyrZi18RQbAB2cUffu)_",
